MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Partners feels like a natural next choice because vocal duets fit the polished, expressive singing I enjoyed in A Musical Affair and Stages.",
    "Beethoven connects with my latest classical listening, while Peter, Paul and Mary's melodic songs and harmonies connect with the familiar songwriting I sought in The Bang Years."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Girl On Fire and Unorthodox Jukebox feel less relevant because I currently want orchestral music and theatrical vocals rather than a contemporary pop sound.",
    "Together, Impressions, Slam Dunk and Another Long Night Out give me too little evidence of the expressive vocals or orchestral sound I want; I would pass because their fit is uncertain."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some pop albums seems to have been stretched into an interest in contemporary pop generally, when the singing and melodic character matter more to me.",
    "A duet theme catches my interest, but that alone does not make an album a choice: for Duets: Re-Working The Catalogue, the performers and songs would determine whether I follow through."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest choice suggests an interest in relaxing classical listening; Beethoven is appealing, but its greater energy means it serves a different mood.",
    "The repeated appeal of expressive singing across Stages, A Musical Affair and Lead With Your Heart matters more to me than simply finding another vocal album."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understand my interest in melodic vocals and classical music, but miss how much my choices depend on mood, performers and the particular style of singing."
}
